1. Project Abstract

Azure Managed Identity Adoption Across an Application Estate is an identity and security project that aims to eliminate the use of Service Principal client secrets for authenticating applications to Azure services. The project implements Azure Managed Identity to provide secretless authentication, allowing Azure-hosted applications to securely obtain access tokens through Microsoft Entra ID without storing or managing credentials.

The project involves identifying applications that currently use Service Principal secrets, migrating supported applications to System-Assigned or User-Assigned Managed Identities, and configuring Azure Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) to provide only the required permissions. The implementation demonstrates secure access to Azure services such as Azure Key Vault, Azure Storage, and Azure SQL.

The project also considers practical migration challenges. Some legacy services may not support Managed Identity and therefore require temporary alternative authentication mechanisms. Cross-tenant authentication scenarios are outside the scope of the project. The final outcome is a working proof of concept demonstrating secretless authentication, reduced credential-management overhead, and improved security for Azure applications.

